"""Synthetic users for the Yellowback devnet: six personas, not a random walk.

`yellowback-devnet up --role ...` starts one of these beside the devnet (`sim start|stop|stats`
drive it by hand). It reads the devnet's `devnet.json` for the two wallet nodes it owns -- the
**population** node, hosting the five minter/holder personas on distinct YED addresses, and
the **liquidator** node, which owns none of their vaults, because claiming someone else's
underwater vault (RED-4 clause (b) through a notice, or clause (a)) is a different path from
an owner redeeming and is the one the attested price actually governs.

Personas (docs/plans/role-based-regtest-plan.md section 3.4; revision 3 item I-3 on why risk
appetite is the term class):

  leveraged     class A (300 %, the shortest terms): the most leveraged tier, the first underwater
                on a downswing; one vault at a time, redeems at maturity
  conservative  class C (500 %, the longest terms): the most collateralised tier; holds two, never
                redeems early (the in-term early-redeem fee is 1 % for C)
  exiter        redeems the moment lockHeight passes; runs yed_sweepcarriers as
                housekeeping
  trader        never mints: moves YED between its addresses (and to the liquidator) with
                yed_send / yed_sendmany
  absentee      mints, then goes quiet: never redeems, never sweeps
  liquidator    (its own node) watches every vault it does not own against theta x debt at the
                attested claim price each block, printing the price at which each becomes
                claimable; claims at once whatever yed_listclaimable says is claimable (the node
                decides: post-term under the pre-plan rules, at any height under the in-term
                claims plan), with the H-9.3 bounds, releases after claimDelay and logs the
                margin; posts yed_claimnotice when a vault is under the emergency ratio and
                claims after EMERGENCY_PERSIST

Every bundle-carrying command (yed_mint, yed_claim, yed_claimnotice) is two-step; each persona
calls it with wait=true and relies on the heartbeat to mine the carrier, so without a heartbeat
the personas simply block (the plan's R1-before-R3 ordering). A refused action is logged and
tallied by its stable identifier (`bundle-insufficient`, `mintpol-…`, `insufficient-yec`, …),
never retried blindly: those refusals are the signal the attestor and pool scenarios exist to
show. The RNG is seeded (`--seed`), so a run is reproducible.

    yellowback-sim run --dir DIR [--seed N] [--profile demo|fast]
    yellowback-sim stats --dir DIR         # the tally, from <dir>/sim-stats.json
"""
